# Copy to .env.local and fill in what you have. Every key is optional. Elsewhere
# degrades to clearly-labelled demo behaviour for anything that's missing.

# --- Conversational guide (Claude) ------------------------------------------
# https://console.anthropic.com/ → API keys. Without it the map, filters and
# Taste Lens still work; the guide panel explains it isn't configured.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Optional model override (default: claude-opus-5-5). For a cheap demo use
# claude-haiku-5-5 (roughly a cent or less per message vs ~10–20¢ on Opus).
# ELSEWHERE_MODEL=claude-haiku-5-5
# Reasoning effort: low | medium | high (default medium; low is cheaper and faster)
# ELSEWHERE_EFFORT=medium

# --- Cultural intelligence (Qloo) -------------------------------------------
# Request a key from Qloo (https://www.qloo.com/ → contact / developer access).
# Without it, "Taste: demo" mode simulates cultural signals from a small fixture.
QLOO_API_KEY=
# Base URL for your key's environment (hackathon keys use https://hackathon.api.qloo.com)
QLOO_API_URL=https://api.qloo.com
# Force demo mode even when a key is present (useful for offline demos)
# QLOO_MODE=demo

# --- Place data --------------------------------------------------------------
# Provider chain: Google Places (if keyed) → Overpass (if configured) → demo snapshot.
# Google Places API (New): enable "Places API (New)" in Google Cloud and create a key.
GOOGLE_PLACES_API_KEY=
# Comma-separated Overpass endpoints. The public overpass-api.de instance rejects
# automated traffic, so point this at your own instance (or a provider you have terms with).
OVERPASS_URL=
# Pin a single provider: google | overpass | demo
# PLACES_PROVIDER=

# Identify the app to OSM services (Nominatim/Overpass usage policies require it)
HTTP_USER_AGENT=Elsewhere/0.1 (you@example.com)
# NOMINATIM_URL=https://nominatim.openstreetmap.org

# --- Routing (Taste Trails) -------------------------------------------------
# Walking/cycling/driving routes and travel times come from OSRM. By default Elsewhere uses
# the FOSSGIS community servers (routing.openstreetmap.de: foot, bike and car profiles),
# fine for development and demos at low volume. For production, run your own OSRM and set:
# OSRM_URL=https://your-osrm.example.com
# (one profile per URL; transit isn't supported and falls back to labelled walking routes)

# --- Map ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Any MapLibre style built on the OpenMapTiles schema works (default: OpenFreeMap Liberty)
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MAP_STYLE_URL=https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/liberty
